openssh-server
# initramfs-tools compresses the initrd with $COMPRESS, and the image sets
# zstd.  --apt-recommends false drops zstd from the transaction (it is only a
# Recommends of initramfs-tools), so every kernel install printed
#   W: No zstd in /usr/bin:/sbin:/bin, using gzip
# and shipped a gzip initrd next to a zstd expectation.  Install it explicitly
# so the compression the configuration asks for actually exists.
zstd
